title: Education & Science
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: psoe_in_government and education_science_timer = 0 and black_thursday_seen = 0
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/EinsteinAlbert.jpg
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Education and Science

Education is one of the Republic's signature causes. Marcelino Domingo's ministry has committed to building thousands of new public schools, sending the Misiones Pedagógicas - traveling teams of teachers, books, and even a projector - into the most isolated villages of rural Spain, and breaking the religious orders' near-monopoly on secondary education. The PSOE has real influence over this program from within the coalition.

[? if major_curriculum: Current educational curriculum - [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +] ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @increase_science
- @structure
- @curriculum
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action


@increase_science
title: Increase funding for scientific research.

<span style="color: #9b0000;">Socialism</span> has always stood for science and rationality. Despite the setbacks of war, dictatorship, and the politicized, often clerically-dominated attitudes of the old university establishment, Spanish science - embodied in the Junta para Ampliación de Estudios and its Residencia de Estudiantes - has real achievements to build on. With expanded funding, we hope to keep building.

- @jae
- @applied
- @medical
- @cut_funding
- @ed_menu: Do not increase research funding.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@jae
title: Fund the Junta para Ampliación de Estudios for basic scientific research.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; kwg_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.3 if economic_growth <= 8; urban_middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.2 if unemployed >= 4; west_relation += 1; science_funding += 1

The Junta para Ampliación de Estudios is one of the more respected scientific and cultural institutions in the country, its Residencia de Estudiantes having hosted the likes of Lorca, Dalí, and Buñuel. Our research program provides it with additional resources to hire and train scholars and conduct fundamental research, based on the researchers' own interests.

@applied
title: Fund applied research in economically useful technologies.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; applied_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth <= 8 and applied_research <= 1; economic_growth += 3 if applied_research > 1; urban_middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.5 if unemployed >= 4; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 1; science_funding += 1

Our research program focuses on collaborating with industry and agriculture to develop useful technologies, creating new research institutions for applied science aimed at economic growth and development.


@medical
title: Fund public-health and medical research.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; medical_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.4 if economic_growth <= 8; urban_middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.2 if unemployed >= 4; science_funding += 1

Our research program focuses on public-health measures and medical research to improve the treatment of disease, especially in the rural south where mortality remains far higher than in the cities.

@cut_funding
title: Cut science funding.
subtitle: +1 budget
choose-if: science_funding >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have not funded science.
on-arrival: budget += 1; science -= 1; science_funding -= 1; applied_research -= 0.33; kwg_research -= 0.33; medical_research -= 0.33; economic_growth -= 0.5; urban_middle_psoe -= 5; industrial_psoe -= 2; izq_rep_relation -= 4; radical_relation -= 2; unemployed += 0.3

We have cut funding for science. This has a negative effect on economic growth, and unemployed researchers are less likely to support the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span>.


@structure
title: Change the structure and funding of education.

Spanish education has traditionally been organized on religious and class lines. The religious orders, above all the Jesuits, control much of secondary education, while working-class children rarely see more than a few years of primary schooling. The universities and the civil service that draws from them lean accordingly conservative and clerical.

- @secularize
- @public_hs
- @school_boards
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organization.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize
title: Break the religious orders' hold on secondary education, per Article 26.
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -1 budget - requires solid coalition support.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and izq_rep_relation >= 40 and radical_relation >= 25
view-if: secularized = 0
go-to: secularize_menu if in_republican_socialist; secularize_2 if not in_republican_socialist

@secularize_menu

Are you sure about this? Even our republican coalition partners are wary of moving too fast on Article 26 - Izquierda Republicana worries it will hand the CEDA a rallying cry, whatever their own anticlerical convictions.

- @secularize_2: Yes, do it.
- @ed_menu: No, do not touch religious education.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize_2
on-arrival: secularized = 1; budget -= 1; catholic_psoe -= 15; catholic_ceda += 10; ceda_relation -= 15; izq_rep_relation += 6*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 3*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5; coalition_dissent += 2 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front

The PSOE and Izquierda Republicana push through legislation enforcing Article 26, closing the door on the religious orders' teaching monopoly and funding secular community schools to replace some of the schools they ran. The CEDA, predictably, treats this as confirmation that the Republic means to destroy the Church.


@public_hs
title: Fund the mass school-building program in working-class and rural areas.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; public_hs += 1; industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5; unemployed -= 0.1; economic_growth += 0.2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent)
max-visits: 3

We have funded thousands of new public schools, part of Domingo's signature program, so that working-class and rural children who would otherwise never see the inside of a classroom can receive an education.


@school_boards
title: Create elected school boards to give local areas more control over education.
on-arrival: school_boards += 1; industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2
view-if: school_boards = 0

We have created local elected school boards, delegating some of the decision-making for local schools to them.


@curriculum
title: Change the educational curriculum.
choose-if: curriculum_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if curriculum_timer > 0 : It is too early to change the curriculum again. ?]

Many <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> believe Spanish education is not fit for the modern era - much of it still follows the rote, disciplinarian, often clerically-supervised traditions of the monarchy, and conservative professors dominate the universities. Nevertheless, there have been real strides in bringing working-class children into the schools.

What should be the major focus of our new curriculum?

- @dem_major
- @science_major
- @human_major
- @vocational_major
- @trad_major
- @ed_menu: Do not change the curriculum now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

# note: education_science is a variable that affects how much education affects economic growth.

@dem_major
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; ceda_relation -= 3; izq_rep_relation += 3*(1-dissent); radical_relation -= 5*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist; pacifism += 1; education_science += 0.3
go-to: curriculum_minor

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic - to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of others. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_major
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist; ceda_relation -= 5; izq_rep_relation += 4*(1-dissent); pce_relation += 3*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 2*(1-dissent)
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this.

@human_major
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "humanist"; izq_rep_relation += 3*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 2*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities - arts, literature, history, and philosophy, in the spirit of the Misiones Pedagógicas' own conviction that culture is a right, not a privilege. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects.

@vocational_major
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "vocational"; radical_relation += 3*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 3*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe -= 1; unemployed -= 0.1; education_science += 0.5
go-to: curriculum_minor

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, teaching the skills most useful for students' future working lives.


@trad_major
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and national tradition
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "traditional"; radical_relation += 5*(1-dissent); ceda_relation += 4*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); pacifism -= 1 if pacifism > 0; pro_republic -= 5; nationalism += 5; education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

The traditional curriculum focuses on ancient history and language, particularly Latin and Greek, alongside rigid discipline.


@curriculum_minor

And what should be a secondary focus of the curriculum?

- @dem_minor
- @science_minor
- @human_minor
- @vocational_minor
- @trad_minor

@dem_minor
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
view-if: major_curriculum != "democratic"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; ceda_relation -= 2; radical_relation -= 3; izq_rep_relation += 2*(1-dissent)

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of other citizens. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_minor
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
view-if: major_curriculum != "scientific"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 0.5; ceda_relation -= 3; izq_rep_relation += 3*(1-dissent); pce_relation += 2*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 2*(1-dissent)

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this.

@human_minor
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
view-if: major_curriculum != "humanist"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "humanist"; urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 3*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 2*(1-dissent)

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects.

@vocational_minor
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
view-if: major_curriculum != "vocational"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "vocational"; education_science += 0.3; radical_relation += 2*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 2*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 2*(1-dissent)

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.


@trad_minor
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and national tradition
view-if: major_curriculum != "traditional"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "traditional"; radical_relation += 2*(1-dissent); ceda_relation += 2*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); pro_republic -= 3; nationalism += 3

The traditional curriculum focuses on ancient history and language (particularly Latin and Greek), as well as rigid discipline.
